 "result": "Saved `scenario.json`.\n\n**Request:** \"Rename the 'Product Team' calendar that's currently checked in my calendar list to 'Eng Product Sync'.\" (writes `calendar_list_entries.summary_override` via `PATCH /users/me/calendarList/{id}`)\n\n**Decoys:**\n- `product_team_mkt` — fact `A:CalendarListEntry.selected`, family F0: a second calendar also named \"Product Team\" but unchecked (selected=false) in the actor's list.\n- `product_team_offsite` — fact `A:Calendar.summary`, family F8: checked, but named \"Product Team Offsite\" (contains the requested name as a substring).\n- `eng_roadmap` — fact `A:Calendar.summary`, family F0: checked, but an unrelated calendar named \"Engineering Roadmap\".\n\nBackground calendars (`us_holidays`, `design_team`) are both unchecked and differently named, so they fail both conditions and don't compete with the decoys. The target is owned by another user (Priya), so the correct write must go through the calendar-list endpoint rather than the owner-only calendar-metadata endpoint.",
